Rework draft PR #7728 ("Bind type-parameter-free members on parameterized JDK call results (#7619)"): branch 7619-java-generic-result-receivers, worktree .mj/lanes/7728, head 88bc6ad595. It is 2,262 commits behind master. Read first: AGENTS.md (CLAUDE.md is a symlink to it): Git rules, Running tests, the coding conventions. Then the PR body and every comment (`gh pr view 7728 -R BrokkAi/bifrost-dev --comments`; if GraphQL fails, use `gh api repos/BrokkAi/bifrost-dev/issues/7728/comments`), and issue #7619.
Phase 1, merge (no rebase):
- `git fetch origin && git merge origin/master`. Known conflicts: crates/bifrost-analysis/src/analyzer/native_points.rs, crates/bifrost-jvm-analysis/src/analyzer/java/native_points.rs, crates/bifrost-store/src/analyzer/resolution/fact_resolution.rs, crates/bifrost-store/src/analyzer/resolution/mounted.rs, icfg.rs and units.rs.
- Resolve the code conflicts by keeping both sides' intent, and record each resolution in the merge message.
- Identity: drop this branch's stale ICFG pair (v101/v100). Take master's pair for now; the coordinator assigns a new one before ready. Keep every POLICY_SUBSTRATE_EPOCH token, in landing order, with its component rows. Re-check any bundle epoch this branch bumped against master and report each one.
Phase 2, the hook port. This shape is DECIDED with session 28c4a33b; do not re-litigate it. #8603 (on master) added a no-op side-effect hook `rules::unresolved_static_owner` with a borrowed `JvmUnresolvedStaticOwner` witness in jvm_context.rs. It runs in the shared evaluator after the common alias and member evaluation and before the external-boundary push, only for a static import with no JLS or common owner, no alias, a non-empty owner and empty open-alias/coverage routes. This branch's import-route member-scope hunk, formerly in java_import_context_parts (~5531-5565: for each selected_java_import_route_gap_reasons(...) reason, record_java_import_member_scope(reason, site_semantic(fragment, source_site), &owner)), moves onto that hook:
- change the hook to `fn unresolved_static_owner(&self, witness: &JvmUnresolvedStaticOwner) -> Option<JvmStaticOwnerScope>`, defaulting to None, with the owner FQN in the witness;
- Java's rules return Some(JvmStaticOwnerScope naming the owner);
- the COMMON assembly does the selected_java_import_route_gap_reasons read and the record write, so writes stay in one place;
- rename the record call JVM-neutrally (for example record_jvm_import_member_scope), because shared assembly code must not name a language.
Delete the old hunk so there is one copy only.
Phase 3, validate in the canonical env (env -u JAVA_HOME -u RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN, BIFROST_OPEN_PACKS_DISABLE=1, parallelism 1, fresh XDG_CACHE_HOME per run with no BIFROST_CACHE_ROOT, eatmydata, nice -n 10, --max-fail 100):
- cargo check on the touched crates;
- the store and jvm-analysis libs;
- the PR's own goldens (golden_java_generic_result_receivers and so on);
- the JVM-filtered root suites (-E 'test(/java|scala|jvm|kotlin/)') in the default and BIFROST_TRIAL_NATIVE_JAVA=1 configurations, compared by first panic with origin/master;
- Clippy -D warnings on the touched crates, fmt, pack drift and the projection dry run.
For every golden line this branch changes against master, give its cause.
STOP after phase 3 and report:
- the merge resolutions;
- the hook-port diff summary;
- any review item from the PR comments that is still open (for example the 2026-10-28 note that `Choices.box(1)` stays incomplete because boxing is phase 2 under JLS 15.12.2.2);
- the validation table.
Commit with multiline messages and the trailer `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`. Do not push. No cloud. Logs go in /tmp/7728/.
